### Implementation Details
<hr class="section-rule lvl-3">

To keep `compose.mk` itself self-contained, the base container for the TUI is actually inlined, and it is unpacked and built only on demand. For the exact specification, see [the source]({{github.repo_url}}/tree/main/compose.mk) and look for the `TUI_COMPOSE_FILE` variable.

Note that the base container is required for a few use-cases that are not, strictly speaking, the TUI.  (For example {{site.api_link('io.figlet',mkdocs)}}.)

To ensure the TUI container is built before trying to use it, use {{site.api_link('tux.require',mkdocs)}} as a prerequisite target.  The TUI container is cached by default after the initial build, but you can force purge/rebuild by using `force=1 ./compose.mk tux.require`.

